window.KB_BODY[62]={"tsb103001":"<h2>Service Tools Procedure Additions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic adds two kits to the cylinder block service tool list. They are (1) Hydraulic Actuator Kit, Part Number 3823621, and (2) Camshaft Bushing Installation and Removal Kit, Part Number 3162253, to Procedure 022-001 (Service Tools) in Section 1 of the C Series Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666003\">3666003</a>.</p>","tsb103008":"<h2>(Bearings, Main) Procedure, General Information Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises a statement about the upper main bearing shells in the General Information Section of the (Bearings, Main) Procedure, Procedure 001-006 for 6C, C8.3, C8.3G, C Gas Plus, and L Gas Plus engines in the C Series Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666003\">3666003</a> and the C8.3G, C Gas Plus, and L Gas Plus Engines, Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, Bulletin 3666206.</p>","tsb103053":"<h2>(Flywheel Housing, REPTO) Procedure, Install Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedure 016-007 (Flywheel Housing, REPTO) to include a step to check for backlash between the Hydrive housing gear and the idler gear. It has been determined that a small amount of backlash <b>must</b> be present for correct operation. A no backlash condition can cause premature component failure.</p>","tsb103054":"<h2>Lubricating Oil Pump Procedure, Multiple Section Revisions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedure 007-031 (Lubricating Oil Pump) in Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666239\">3666239</a>, Signature™, ISX, and QSX15 Service Manual, to include instructions to reuse the external idler gear capscrew.</p><p>This capscrew is <b>not</b> listed for sale in the lubricating oil pump option. To obtain a replacement the capscrew, the complete lubricating oil pump option <b>must</b> be purchased.</p>","tsb103057":"<h2>Overhead Set (OBC) Procedure, General Information Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the General Information Section in Procedure 003-006, Overhead Set (OBC), in the Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, QSK23 Series Engine, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021375\">4021375</a>.</p>","tsb103072":"<h2>Lubricating Oil System Specifications, Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic updates Procedure 018-017 (Lubricating Oil System) in the specifications section of the Signature™, ISX, and QSX15 manuals listed above.</p><ul><li>The update changes the lubricating oil pan capacity for power generation applications to 90.8 liters [24 gal].</li></ul>","tsb103083":"<h2>QSK23 Tier 2 Engine Introduction</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>The purpose of this Service/Parts Topic is to introduce the QSK23 Tier 2 Engine (engine family 89). The QSK23 is a 23 liter, 4-valve head, 1 pump-1 loop, air-to-air charge air cooler (ATA-CAC), inline 6-cylinder diesel engine, certified to U.S. EPA Tier 2 emissions. The QSK23 fills the horsepower node between the QSK19 and QST30, with ratings between 760 to 950 hp for industrial applications, and 880 and 1220 hp for power generation applications. This engine is fully electronically controlled, with a displacement of 23.15 liters [1413 cu in] targeted at various applications within the mining, construction, and power generation markets. The QSK23 is a Cummins® branded engine and all current Cummins Inc. warranty coverages and guidelines apply.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Engine Envelope/Weight Comparison</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td></td><td>QSK23 Cummins® Turbo Technologies Turbocharger Tier 2</td><td>QSK23 Schwitzer Turbocharger</td></tr><tr><td>Height above Crankshaft Centerline</td><td>1159 mm [45.6 inch]</td><td>1133 mm [44.6 inch]</td></tr><tr><td>Overall Engine Height</td><td>1720 mm [67.7 inch]</td><td>1694 mm [66.7 inch]</td></tr><tr><td>Overall Length - Rear of flywheel housing to fan mounting pilot face</td><td>1939 mm [76.3 inch]</td><td>1939 mm [76.3 inch]</td></tr><tr><td>Overall Width</td><td>1046 mm [41.2 inch]</td><td>1068 [42 inch]</td></tr><tr><td>Weight (dry - lbs)</td><td>2858 kg [6300 lb]</td><td>2858 kg [6300 lb]</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Training for the QSK23 Tier 2 is contained in Cummins® Virtual College training modules. This will be part of the High Horsepower Virtual College.</p>","tsb103091":"<h2>(Valve Guide, Cylinder Head) Procedure, Inspect for Reuse Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the Inspect for Reuse section of Procedure 002-017 (Valve Guide, Cylinder Head) in Section 2 of the C Series Engines Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666003\">3666003</a>.</p>","tsb103097":"<h2>Piston and Connecting Rod Assembly Procedure, Remove Section Revision; Connecting Rod Procedure, Measure Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedures 001-054 (Piston and Connecting Rod Assembly) and 001-014 (Connecting Rod) in Section 1 of the Service Manual, QSK45 and QSK60, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>.</p><p>The piston and connecting rod assembly procedure was revised for split angle split connecting rods <b>only</b> and the connecting rod procedure torque values were revised.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and is <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb103098":"<h2>Fuel Manifold (Supply) Procedure, Multiple Section Revisions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises multiple sections in Procedure 006-022 (Fuel Manifold (Supply)) in Section 6 of the QSK 45 and QSK 60 Series Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>.</p>","tsb103100":"<h2>Service Tools Addition</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic adds the injector protrusion gauge to the Cylinder Head Service Tools Procedure in the K19 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021499\">4021499</a>.</p>","tsb103101":"<h2>Cylinder Head Procedure, Assemble Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic adds the injector protrusion gauge, Part Number 4919196, to the Assemble section of Procedure 002-004 (Cylinder Head) in the K19 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021499\">4021499</a>.</p>","tsb103129":"<h2>Piston and Cylinder Liner Procedure, Multiple Section Revisions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedure 001-045 (Piston and Cylinder Liner) in Section 1 of the QSK45 and QSK60 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>.</p><p>An additional cylinder liner removal tool and related usage has been added, in addition to the inclusion of a straight torque value for tightening the connecting rods when working through the hand hole covers.</p>","tsb103132":"<h2>Piston Procedure, Clean and Inspect for Reuse Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedure 001-043 (Piston) in the QSK45 and QSK60 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>. The revision includes new minimum reuse limits for the top piston ring groove in the Ring Groove Wear Limits table. The top ring groove wear limits have been modified to a minimum specification of 159.10 mm [6.264 in].</p>","tsb103140":"<h2>Camshaft Bushings Procedure, Multiple Section Revisions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts topic changes specifications in multiple sections of Procedure 001-010 (Camshaft Bushings) in Section 1 of the K19 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021499\">4021499</a>. The camshaft bushing removal and installation tool part numbers were revised.</p>","tsb103145":"<h2>Maintenance Schedule Revision, Overhead Set</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedure 102-002 (Maintenance Schedule) to remove the Overhead Set - Adjust procedure from the maintenance schedule in Section 2 of the Operation and Maintenance Manual QSK23 Series Engine, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021374\">4021374</a>.</p>","tsb103184":"<h2>Symptom Tree t105 (Lubricating Oil Pressure Low) Revisions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Symptom Tree t105 (Lubricating Oil Pressure Low) to add a differential pressure drop test and revise the tree to address oil filter plugging.</p>","tsb103189":"<h2>Symptom Tree t103-56 (Lubricating Oil Filter Plugged), Major Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Symptom Tree t103-56 (Lubricating Oil Filter Plugged) to give more specific instructions as to when the unit should return to service. Several steps have also been modified and added for clarity.</p>","tsb103192":"<h2>Symptom Tree t021 (Coolant Loss - Internal), Cause Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Symptom Tree t021 (Coolant Loss - Internal). The revision changes the procedure reference for inspecting the air compressor air lines. This change improves troubleshooting logic by directing users to Procedure 012-007 (Air Compressor Cylinder Head, Single Cylinder) for an initial check of the air lines instead of Procedure 012-014 (Air Compressor) for air compressor removal.</p>","tsb103209":"<h2>Eliminator™ Filter Procedure, Assemble Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic announces a revision to the Assemble Section of Procedure 007-067 (Eliminator™ Filter). The hydraulic motor mounting capscrew torque value has been revised.</p>","tsb103220":"<h2>Fan Drive Idler Arm Assembly Procedure, Assembly Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This purpose of this Service/Parts Topic is revise the assembly section in Procedure 008-029 (Fan Drive Idler Arm Assembly). The assembly torque specifications in the summary now match the specifications in the step.</p>","tsb103221":"<h2>Pre-Lubricating Oil Pump Procedure, Install Section Revisions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the mounting bracket capscrew torque value in the Install section of Procedure 007-063 (Pre-Lubricating Oil Pump).</p>","tsb103222":"<h2>Aftercooler Assembly Procedure, Assemble Section Revisions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic announces revisions to the Assemble section of Procedure 010-002 (Aftercooler Assembly).</p><p>The revisions clarify the Assemble section of the procedure by removing information about the installation of the lower cooler element gasket.</p><p>Only one gasket is used; between the aftercooler support and aftercooler cover.</p>","tsb103223":"<h2>Maintenance Schedule Addition</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedure 102-002 (Maintenance Schedule) to include a recommended injector replacement at engine half life to rebuild.</p>","tsb103224":"<h2>Procedure 006-026 (Injector), Replace Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedure 006-026 (Injector) in Section 9 of the Operation and Maintenance Manual QSK19 and QSK19 CM850 Modular Common Rail System, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666120\">3666120</a>. This procedure recommends injector replacement at engine half life to rebuild.</p>","tsb103226":"<h2>Integrated Fuel System Module (IFSM) Procedure, Multiple Section Revisions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the Disassemble and Assemble sections of Procedure 005-073 (Integrated Fuel System Module (IFSM)) in Section 5. Information for disassembly and assembly were included for the CM570 (IFSM).</p>","tsb103229":"<h2>Procedure 006-026 (Injector), Replace Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic adds the Procedure 006-026 (Injector) to Section 10 of the Operation and Maintenance Manual K38, K50, QSK38 and QSK50, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3810497\">3810497</a>. This procedure recommends injector replacement at engine half life to rebuild for both the mechanically and electronically actuated injectors.</p>","tsb103232":"<h2>(Crankshaft Seal, Rear) Procedure, Multiple Section Revisions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedure 001-024 (Crankshaft Seal, Rear) in Section 1. Revisions include clarification on proper orientation and installation of the rear crankshaft seal and spacer used for installation. In addition, measurement specifications for protusion and squareness for the rear crankshaft seal have been added to make sure of the proper installation depth and orientation.</p>","tsb103247":"<h2>Fault Code 259, Major Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic introduces major revisions to Fault Code 259.</p>","tsb103262":"<h2>Fault Code 155, New</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic introduces Fault Code 155.</p>","tsb103265":"<h2>Multiple Group 01 Procedure Revisions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic documents revisions to Procedures 001-026 (Cylinder Block), 001-037 (Idler Gear, Camshaft (Left Bank)), 001-038 (Idler Gear, Camshaft (Right Bank)), 001-039 (Idler Gear, Hydraulic Pump), and 001-040 (Idler Gear, Water Pump). The revisions include specifications changes in the Clean and Inspect for Reuse section.</p>","tsb103267":"<h2>Rocker Lever Assembly Procedure, Torque Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic documents a revision to the torque value of the rocker lever assembly mounting capscrews in the Install section of Procedure 003-009 (Rocker Lever Assembly).</p>","tsb103271":"<h2>Fuel Drain Lines Procedure, Multiple Section Revisions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic documents the addition of the removal and installation process for the new style fuel drain line bracket to the Remove and Install sections of Procedure 006-013 (Fuel Drain Lines).</p>","tsb103273":"<h2>Air Leaks, Compressed Air System Procedure Addition</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This purpose of this Service/Parts Topic is to revise Procedure 012-019 (Air Leaks, Compressed Air System) in order to include this procedure in Section 4 of the Operation and Maintenance Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666260\">3666260</a>. This procedure needs to be performed for all compressed air systems to prevent carbon build-up and possible failure of the compressed air system.</p>","tsb103274":"<h2>(Air Leaks, Compressed Air System) Procedure Addition</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This purpose of this Service/Parts Topic is to revise the Maintenance Schedule in order to include Procedure 012-019 (Air Leaks, Compressed Air System) into Section 4 of the Operation and Maintenance Manual QSK45 and QSK60 Series Engines, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666260\">3666260</a>, so that it is checked on a regular basis. This procedure needs to be performed for all compressed air systems to prevent carbon build-up and possible failure of the compressed air system.</p>","tsb103281":"<h2>Alternator Drive Pulley Procedure, Remove Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the Remove section of Procedure 009-010 in Section 9 of the K19 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021499\">4021499</a>.</p>","tsb103283":"<h2>Engine Performance Troubleshooting Tree, Guided Step 5B Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Guided Step 5B in the Engine Performance Troubleshooting Tree, adding a note about repeating the test step if more than one injuector is malfunctioning.</p>","tsb103287":"<h2>Maintenance Schedule, Radiator Pressure Cap Check Addition</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedure 102-002 (Maintenance Schedule) in Section 2 of the Signature™ and ISX Operation and Maintenance Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666251\">3666251</a>, to add the Radiator Pressure Cap maintenance check. The manual is being revised to ensure the radiator pressure cap is functioning correctly. The system <b>must</b> maintain pressure to make sure of proper engine performance.</p>","tsb103289":"<h2>Gear Cover Trunion Sleeve, New Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic introduces a new Procedure 001-030 (Gear Cover Trunion Sleeve) in Section 1, in the QSK45 and QSK60 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>.</p>","tsb103303":"<h2>Piston and Connecting Rod Assembly Procedure (Section Addition), and Connecting Rod Procedure (Section Revision).</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topics adds a Clean and Inspect for Reuse section in Procedure 001-054 (Piston and Connecting Rod Assembly) and removes a torque table in the Bend and Twist Inspect section in Procedure 001-014 (Connecting Rod).</p>","tsb103306":"<h2>Fuel Pump Procedure, Multple Section Revisions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedure 005-016 in Section 5 to include information about painting the fuel pump after it is installed.</p>","tsb103307":"<h2>Injector Procedure, Multple Section Revisions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedure 006-026 (Injector) in Section 6 to includ information about painting the exposed portion of the electronically actuated injector to prevent the formation of rust and corrosion.</p>","tsb103332":"<h2>STC Oil Manifold Procedure, Install Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the Install section in Procedure 006-038 (STC Oil Manifold) for the K19 engine. Loctite™ 271 is be applied to the capscrews before installation, to prevent loosening.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and is <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb103335":"<h2>Lubricating Oil Leaks Procedure, Initial Check Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedure 007-024 in Section 7 of the C Series Engines Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666003\">3666003</a>. A black light kit has been added to aid in troubleshooting external oil leaks.</p>","tsb103341":"<h2>Maintenance Schedule, Radiator Pressure Cap Check Addition</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedure 102-002 (Maintenance Schedule) in Section 2 of the ISX Owners Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4960314\">4960314</a>, to add the Radiator Pressure Cap maintenance check. The manual is being revised to make sure the radiator pressure cap is functioning correctly. The system <b>must</b> maintain pressure to make sure of proper engine performance.</p>","tsb103344":"<h2>Multiple Group 02 Procedure Revisions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedures 002-004 (Cylinder Head) and 002-016 (Valve Guide Seal, Cylinder Head) in the Signature™, ISX and QSX15 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666239\">3666239</a>. The revision includes the addition of detailed steps for the new four valve spring compressor tool, Part Number 4919358.</p>","tsb103345":"<h2>New Four Valve Spring Compressor Tool</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic introduces a new four valve spring compressor tool, Part Number 4919358, for use on Signature™, ISX, and QSX15 engines. See Figure 1. The new tool has been revised to accommodate future products. The new four valve spring compressor tool, Part Number 4919358, replaces four valve spring compressor tool, Part Number 3162986. The new tool is backwards compatible with all previous Signature™, ISX, and QSX15 engines which utilized tool, Part Number 3162986.</p><p>This Service/Parts Topic also revises Procedure 022-001 (Service Tools) in Section 2 for the Signature™, ISX, and QSX15 engines.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and is <b>not</b> subject to Campaign or TRP.</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22c00350.png\" alt=\"22c00350.png\"></figure><p>Figure 1</p>","tsb103354":"<h2>Camshaft Bushings Procedure, Major Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises multiple sections of Procedure 001-010 (Camshaft Bushings).</p>","tsb103361":"<h2>(Exhaust Manifold, Dry) Procedure, Install Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the Install Section of Procedure 011-007 (Exhaust Manifold, Dry) in the Service Manual, QSK45 and QSK60, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>. The installation of the lockplates has been revised.</p>","tsb103366":"<h2>Revision, Engine Fan Does Not Operate or Operates Erratically Symptom Tree</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises symptom tree T046 (Engine Fan Does Not Operate or Operates Erratically) for the Signature™, ISX, and QSX15 Electronic Control System Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, Bulletin 3666259. The symptom tree title has been modified to include the fan operating continuously (Engine Fan Does Not Operate, Operates Erratically, Or Operates Continuously). Multiple tree nodes have also been added for troubleshooting this condition.</p>","tsb103372":"<h2>Fault Code 418 Addition</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic adds Fault Code 418 (Water-In-Fuel Indicator - Data Valid but Above Normal Operational Range - Least Severe Level) to the Signature™, ISX, and QSX15 Electronic Control System Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, Bulletin 3666259.</p>","tsb103373":"<h2>Service Tool Addition, Lubricating Oil System</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This document adds the Oil Cooler Leak Test Kit, Part Number 4918200, to Service Tools in Section 7.</p><p>The oil cooler leak test kit is used to pressurize the oil cooler assembly in order to check for leaks. It is used with air pressure regulator, Part Number 3164231 or equivalent. Use the following procedure in the Signature™, ISX, and QSX15 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666239\">3666239</a>. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/10-007-003-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-003 in Section 7.</a></p><h3>Document History</h3>","tsb103392":"<h2>Cylinder Head Procedure, Clean and Inspect for Reuse Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic adds a step to the Clean and Inspect for Reuse section of Procedure 002-004 (Cylinder Head). A check for cracked exhaust port divider has been added.</p>","tsb103400":"<h2>Cylinder Head Procedure, Assemble Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises procedure 002-004 (Cylinder Head) for the QSK45 and QSK60 CM850 MCRS engines. The instruction to repair the cylinder head injector seats, if found out of specification, has been removed from the Assemble section for mechanical and electronically actuated injectors.</p>","tsb103401":"<h2>(Bearings, Main) Procedure, Remove Section Revision and Crankshaft Procedure, Multiple Section Additions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises procedures 001-006 (Bearings, Main) and 001-016 (Crankshaft) for the QSK45 and QSK60 engines.</p><p>The Remove section has been revised for procedure 001-006 in Section 1. Preparatory and Finishing sections have been added to procedure 001-016 in Section 1.</p>","tsb103420":"<h2>Cylinder Block and Liner Seats Procedure, Major Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises multiple sections of Procedure 001-027 (Cylinder Block and Liner Seats).</p>","tsb103421":"<h2>Cylinder Block Procedure, Major Revision, and Removal of Cylinder Liner Bore Concentricity Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic introduces a complete revision of Procedure 001-026 (Cylinder Block) and removes Procedure 001-070 (Cylinder Liner Bore Concentricity).</p>","tsb103429":"<h2>(Bracket, Accessory) Procedure, Install Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the Install Section of Procedure 001-082 (Bracket Accessory) in Section 1 of the Signature™, ISX, and QSX15 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666239\">3666239</a>. An instruction to apply a heavy moly grease to the area of contact between the brace and the cylinder head has been added.</p>","tsb103435":"<h2>Aftercooler Assembly Procedure, Install Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the hose clamp torque in the Install section of Procedure 010-002 (Aftercooler Assembly).</p>","tsb103441":"<h2>Fault Code 255, Major Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises all of the troubleshooting steps for Fault Code 255 (Fuel Shutoff Valve Solenoid Supply Circuit) in Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, Electronic Control System, Signature™, ISX, and QSX15, Bulletin 3666259.</p>","tsb103446":"<h2>Fault Code 449, Component Location Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic updates the Hydraulic Fuel System Component location section of Fault Code 449. The changes improve component identification.</p>","tsb103458":"<h2>Maintenance Schedule, Crankcase Breather Element Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Section 7 with the removal of the 1 year specification from the section title in Procedure 102-002 (Maintenance Schedule) in the Signature™ and ISX Operation and Maintenance Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666251\">3666251</a>. The crankcase breather element maintenance, in Section 7, is an emissions related component and can <b>not</b> have a time limit specified for a service interval. The customer <b>must</b> use the mileage or hours as a guideline.</p>","tsb103497":"<h2>Flywheel Housing Procedure, Install Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic adds a torque value for the rear engine mounts in the Install section of Procedure 016-006 (Flywheel Housing) in Section 16.</p>","tsb103499":"<h2>Cylinder Head Procedure, Multiple Section Revisions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedure 002-004 (Cylinder Head) in Section 2 for K19 engines in Service Bulletin, K19, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021499\">4021499</a>.</p><p>The use of the injector protrusion gauge, Part Number 4919196, in the Assemble section has been corrected.</p>","tsb103509":"<h2>Lubricating Oil Leaks Procedure, Initial Check Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the Initial Check section in Procedure 007-024 (Lubricating Oil Leaks). The engine is to be operated under load, if necessary, to duplicate the leak conditions.</p>","tsb103512":"<h2>Coolant Thermostat Procedure, Install Section Revisions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the installation torque value for the new QSK60 thermostat clamping plates and cover plates. This is the same thermostat housing used on the QSK60 with electronically actuated injectors.</p>","tsb103513":"<h2>Turbocharger Procedure, V-Band Clamp Torque Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the torque value for the V-band clamp on the HX02 turbocharger in the Assemble section of Procedure 010-033 (Turbocharger) in the QSK45 and QSK60 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>.</p>","tsb103516":"<h2>Coolant Loss Troubleshooting Symptom Trees, Obsolescence and Revisions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic announces the obsolescence of Troubleshooting Symptom Tree t019 and the revision of Troubleshooting Symptom Trees t021 and t025. These changes improve troubleshooting logic for coolant loss.</p><p>The Coolant Loss Troubleshooting Symptom Tree t019 was removed because the tree steps are addressed in other, more applicable Troubleshooting Symptom Trees.</p><p>Revisions to Coolant Loss - Internal Troubleshooting Symptom Tree t021 include the following:</p><ul><li>Changes to the order of the steps</li><li>Addition of a check for a leaking Auxiliary Power Unit</li><li>Removal of the Pressure Test step</li><li>Change in the final step that identifies the Cause as &#x27;Base engine problem&#x27; and the Correction as &#x27;Refer to Cummins Inc. and request additional technical assistance&#x27;.</li></ul><p>Revisions to Coolant in the Lubricating Oil Troubleshooting Symptom Tree t025 include the following:</p><ul><li>Changes to the order of the steps</li><li>Addition of a check for damaged injector o-rings or damaged sleeve</li><li>Removal of the cylinder liner is corroded or cracked step</li><li>Removal of the cylinder block is cracked or porous step</li><li>Change in the final step that identifies the Cause as &#x27;Base engine problem&#x27; and the Correction as &#x27;Refer to Cummins Inc. and request additional technical assistance&#x27;.</li></ul>","tsb103526":"<h2>Maintenance Schedule Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedure 102-002 (Maintenance Schedule) in Section 2 of the above listed manuals, to add the Radiator Pressure Cap maintenance check. The manuals are being revised to make certain the radiator pressure cap is functioning correctly. The system <b>must</b> maintain pressure to make sure of proper engine performance.</p>","tsb103552":"<h2>Troubleshooting Symptom Trees, Multiple Step Revisions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic announces multiple changes to the Troubleshooting Symptom Trees T101 (Lubricating Oil in the Fuel) and T102 (Lubricating Oil Consumption Excessive) in the Signature™, ISX and QSX15 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666239\">3666239</a>.</p><p>Troubleshooting Symptom Tree T101 (Lubricating Oil in the Fuel), has been modified to include steps for performing a dye test before checking for asphaltines in dark fuel, inspecting the cylinder head injector bore, replacing the upper plunger seal, and inspecting the Integrated Fuel System Module (IFSM) mounting gasket before leak testing the fuel passages.</p><p>Troubleshooting Symptom Tree T102 (Lubricating Oil Consumption Excessive) has been updated to include the dye test for lubricating oil in the fuel, replacement of the upper injector seals, and replacement of the injectors.</p>","tsb103579":"<h2>Symptom Tree t092 (Fuel in the Lubricating Oil), Cause and Correction Additions and Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic updates Symptom Tree t092 (Fuel in the Lubricating Oil) to improve troubleshooting logic. Steps have been moved and added to address the following:</p><ul><li>Fuel pump and injector checks were placed before fuel line restriction checks. The improved tree now places the fuel line restriction check prior to the fuel pump and injector checks.</li><li>There was <b>not</b> a step to check the injectors for blown or missing plug balls. The improved tree now includes this check.</li></ul>","tsb103592":"<h2>Symptom Trees t021 (Coolant Loss) - Internal) and t025 (Coolant in the Lubricating Oil), Service Practice Clarifications</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Troubleshooting Symptom Tree t021 (Coolant Loss - Internal) and t025 (Coolant in the Lubricating Oil) to clarify the action to be taken when the injectors are removed for inspection.</p>","tsb103619":"<h2>Fault Code 2727, Guided Step 2D Addition</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic adds Guided Step 2D to Fault Code 2727, in Section TF of the Troubleshooting and Repair Manual QSK38, QSK50 and QSK60 CM850 Modular Common Rail System, Bulletin 4021533.</p>","tsb103627":"<h2>Engine Performance Troubleshooting Tree, Addition of Guided Step 9I.</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic adds Guided Step 9I (Check for a damaged vibration damper.) to the Engine Performance Troubleshooting Tree in Section TT in the Signature™, ISX, and QSX15 Service Manual, Bulletins <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666239\">3666239</a>.</p>","tsb103634":"<h2>Symptom Tree t047 (Engine Noise Excessive), Reordering of Cause and Correction Steps</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Symptom Tree t047 (Engine Noise Excessive). The sequence of the Cause and Correction steps has been rearranged.</p>","tsb103635":"<h2>Fault Code 393, Guided Step 1A and 1B Revisions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Fault Code 393, Step 1A and 1B in the Signature™, ISX, and QSM15 Electronic Control System Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, Bulletin 3666259.</p>","tsb103650":"<h2>Fault Code 434, Guided Step 4C Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Fault Code 434, Unswitched Battery Supply Circuit, in the &#x27;Action&#x27; section in Guided Step 4C, to revise the pin numbers listed for exclusion in the short circuit check.</p>","tsb103672":"<h2>Maintenance Schedule Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the Maintenance Schedule, removing the &#x27;Crankshaft and clearance - Inspect/Measure&#x27; in Section 6.</p>","tsb103790":"<h2>Crankshaft Procedure, Remove and Install Section Revisions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the remove, install, preparatory and finishing steps in Procedure 001-016 (Crankshaft) in the troubleshooting and repair manual.</p>","tsb103793":"<h2>Cylinder Block Procedure, Inspect for Reuse Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic informs the field of the addition of the main bearing bore diameter dimensions in the Inspect for Resuse section in Procedure 001-026 (Cylinder Block) in Section 1 of the Signature™, ISX, and QSX15 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666239\">3666239</a>.</p>","tsb103804":"<h2>Cylinder Block and Liner Seats Procedure, Measure Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the Measure section of Procedure 001-027 (Cylinder Block and Liner Seats) for Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>. The minimum specification for the Counterbore Diameter - Lower Press Fit Diameter has been changed from a specification of 181.47 mm [7.144 in] to a new specification of 181.74 mm [7.155 in].</p>","tsb103815":"<h2>Fuel Pump Procedure, Multiple Section Revisions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic updates the Install Section of Procedure 005-016 (Fuel Pump) in Section 5, to include a tightening sequence to the torque specifications.</p>","tsb103816":"<h2>New Lift Pump</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic introduces a new lift pump for the QST30 engine and supersedes Service/Parts Topic 09T5-4.</p><p>The new lift pump has a hardened gerotor with an improved tolerance for debris. The new lift pump, Part Number 4975617, went into production with engine serial number (ESN) First 37240363.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Old Part Number</th><th>New Part Number</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>4975518</td><td>4975617</td><td>PUMP, FUEL TRANSFER</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and is <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb103819":"<h2>Cylinder Block Procedure, Head Deck Surface Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the deck height measurements in the Head Deck Surface section of Procedure 001-026 (Cylinder Block) in Section 1 of the QSK45 and QSK60 Series Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>.</p>","tsb103825":"<h2>Cylinder Block Service Tools Addition</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic adds a new service tool, Part Number 4919357, to Procedure 022-001 (Service Tools). This new tool is used to remove main bearings caps.</p>","tsb103832":"<h2>Service Tool Procedure, Cylinder Block Capscrew Thread Repair Service Tools Added</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedure 022-001_01 (Service Tools) to include the tool part numbers required to complete the cylinder head capscrew thread repair.</p>","tsb103845":"<h2>Crankshaft Procedure, Clean and Inspect for Reuse Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Topics revises Procedure 001-016 in Section 1 to add the following statement:</p><p>Inspect the crankshaft for dynamic balancing marks. One or more of the crankshaft counterweights will contain a drilled hole or drilled start point indicating that the crankshaft has been balanced. NOTE – this applies to engines built March 2009 or later <b>only</b>.</p><p>This will allow for an easy check of the crankshaft to make sure it is balanced.</p>","tsb103847":"<h2>New Lubricating Oil Cooler Mounting Stud Gasket</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic introduces a new lubricating oil cooler mounting stud gasket for Industrial and Power Generator QSK45, QSK60, and QSK78 engines.</p><p>This is a product improvement and not subject to campaign.</p><p>The new gasket is an edge-molded gasket which has improved sealing capability.</p><p>The new oil cooler stud gasket, Part Number <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3637730\">3637730</a>, replaces the oil cooler stud gasket, Part Number <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3630969\">3630969</a>, on <b>all</b> QSK45, QSK60, and QSK78 engines. <b>Only</b> use a new oil cooler stud gasket, Part Number <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3637730\">3637730</a>, for repairs.</p><p>The old oil cooler stud gasket, Part Number <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3630969\">3630969</a>, is a paper gasket. The new gasket is an edge-molded gasket.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Procedure 007-045 (Lubricating Oil Cooler Cover) is being revised using three separate Service/Parts Topics to include the use of Loctite™ 271, Part Number 3375068, on oil cooler stud threads due to the introduction of the edge-molded gasket. The following bulletins are affected:</p></div></div><ul><li>QSK78 Series Engines Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, Bulletin 3666727</li><li>Industrial QSK45G and QSK60G Series Engines Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, Bulletin 4021383</li><li>QSK45 and QSK60 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>.</li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/07601238.png\" alt=\"07601238.png\"></figure><p>Old Paper Oil Cooler Stud Gasket, Part Number <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3630969\">3630969</a> (left) and New Edge-mounted Oil Cooler Stud Gasket, Part Number <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3637730\">3637730</a> (right)</p><p>During installation, use Loctite™ 271, Part Number 3375968, sparingly on the oil cooler stud threads.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Oil Cooler Stud Gasket</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Engine</td><td>Old Part Number</td><td>New Part Number</td><td>Part</td></tr><tr><td>QSK45, QSK60, QSK78</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3630969\">3630969</a></td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3637730\">3637730</a></td><td>Gasket, Oil Cooler Stud</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Production Dates and Engine Serial Number First</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Engine</td><td>Production Dates</td><td>Engine Serial Number First</td></tr><tr><td>QSK45 QSK60 QSK78</td><td>30 January 2009 29 January 2009 12 November 2008</td><td>33176552 33177413 66301173</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","tsb103848":"<h2>New IMO Fuel Pump and Kits</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and is <b>not</b> subject to campaign or temporary repair practice (TRP).</p></div></div><p>This Service/Parts Topic describes an issue with the 2004 release of the IMO fuel pump for the following engines:</p><ul><li>QSK23 Industrial and Power Gen</li><li>QSK45 Industrial and Power Gen</li><li>QSK60 Industrial, Power Gen, and Marine</li><li>QSK78 Industrial and Power Gen.</li></ul><p>When the new fuel pump was released the old part numbers for the pumps were <b>not</b> correctly obsoleted. This Service/Parts Topic informs the field that the old part numbers are obsolete and should no longer be ordered.</p><p>The new IMO fuel pump that was released has a design change that places the weep hole in a different location. The location is dependant on both the type of engine and the application. Reference Table 1 for more information:</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Part Number Changes</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Part Name</td><td>Old Part Number</td><td>New Part Number</td><td>Engine Family</td></tr><tr><td>Pump, Fuel</td><td>4062157</td><td>4903531</td><td>QSK23</td></tr><tr><td>Pump, Fuel</td><td>4062157</td><td>4603530</td><td>QSK45</td></tr><tr><td>Pump, Fuel</td><td>4062156</td><td>4903532</td><td>QSK60</td></tr><tr><td>Pump, Fuel</td><td>4062155</td><td>4903533</td><td>Not Used</td></tr><tr><td>Pump, Fuel</td><td>4061675</td><td>4903534</td><td>QSK78</td></tr><tr><td>Kit, Housing Parts</td><td>4087914</td><td>4903561</td><td>QSK23</td></tr><tr><td>Kit, Housing Parts</td><td>4087914</td><td>4903562</td><td>QSK45</td></tr><tr><td>Kit, Housing Parts</td><td>4076762</td><td>4903563</td><td>QSK60</td></tr><tr><td>Kit, Housing Parts</td><td>4076761</td><td>4903564</td><td>Not Used</td></tr><tr><td>Kit, Housing Parts</td><td>4076760</td><td>4903565</td><td>QSK78</td></tr><tr><td>Kit, Housing Parts</td><td>4087971</td><td>4903566</td><td>QSK23</td></tr><tr><td>Kit, Front Cover Parts</td><td>4087971</td><td>4903567</td><td>QSK45, QSK60, and QSK78</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>The weep hole relocation eliminates the low levels of external weep hole leakage by increasing the weep hole reservoir volume and increasing the evaporation rate by facing the weep hole toward the block. The weep hole moves from the 6 o&#x27;clock to the 9 o&#x27;clock position on the bottom of the fuel pump.</p>","tsb103850":"<h2>Lubricating Oil Cooler Cover Procedure, Install Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the Install section of Procedure 007-045 (Lubricating Oil Cooler Cover) in the QSK45 and QSK60 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>, to include the use of Loctite™ 271, Part Number 3375068, on the oil cooler stud threads on the oil cooler cover. This change is due to the introduction of the edge-molded oil cooler stud gasket.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The new lubricating oil cooler mounting stud gasket is being introduced with a separate Service/Parts Topic. Also, Procedure 007-045 (Lubricating Oil Cooler Cover) in the following bulletins is being revised using two separate Service/Parts Topics:</p></div></div><ul><li>QSK78 Series Engines Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, Bulletin 3666727</li><li>Industrial QSK45G and QSK60G Series Engines Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, Bulletin 4021383.</li></ul>","tsb103852":"<h2>(Bearings, Connecting Rod) Procedure, Connecting Rod Bearing Thickness Specification Revisions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the Clean and Inspect for Reuse section of Procedure 001-005 (Bearings, Connecting Rod) to reflect the different connecting rod bearing thickness specifications for the new and old bearings.</p>","tsb103857":"<h2>Lubricating Oil Filter (Spin-On) Procedure, Measure Section Addition</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic adds a Measure section to Procedure 007-013 (Lubricating Oil Filter (Spin-On)). This new section provides part numbers and instructions for measuring the lubricating oil filter differential pressure.</p>","tsb103877":"<h2>Cylinder Head Procedure, Clean and Inspect for Reuse Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>The purpose of the Service/Parts Topic is to introducethe changes to the Clean and Inspect for Reuse Section of Procedure 002-004 (Cylinder Head) in the Signature™, ISX, and QSX15 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666239\">3666239</a>. These changes include adding an inspection of the injector bores. Previously, <b>only</b> the combustion surface and valves were inspected.</p>","tsb103878":"<h2>Injector Procedure, Disassemble and Assemble Section Revisions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic announces changes to the Disassemble and Assemble Sections in Procedure 006-026 (Injector) in the Signature™, ISX, and QSX15 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666239\">3666239</a>. The procedure presently <b>only</b> includes instructions for replacing the upper injector seal on injectors with roll pin retained load rings. The revised procedure adds the information to replace the upper injector seals on injectors with clip retained load rings.</p>","tsb103897":"<h2>Camshaft Procedure, Measure Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedure 001-008 (Camshaft) to provide updated camshaft wear limit specifications and improve the readability of the specification tables.</p>","tsb103905":"<h2>Cooling System Procedure, Fill Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revise the Fill section of Procedure 008-018 (Cooling System) in the Signature, ISX and QSX15 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666239\">3666239</a>.</p><p>The changes provide new information in the procedure regarding the location and type of manual bleed valve(s) or pipe plug(s) installed on certain chassis.</p>","tsb103911":"<h2>Turbocharger Procedure, Install Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the Install section torque value for the standard and Spiralock® nuts.</p><ul><li>ISX Automotive CM570, QSX13 CM570 and Power Generation CM570</li></ul><p>The torque value for the standard nut was changed from 60 N•m [44 ft-lb] to 61 N•m [45 ft-lb]. The torque value for the Spiralock® nut was changed from 60 N•m [44 ft-lb] to 81 N•m [60 ft-lb].</p><ul><li>Automotive CM870</li></ul><p>The mounting nut torque was changed from 88 N•m [65 ft-lb] to 102 N•m [75 ft-lb].</p>","tsb103916":"<h2>Lubricating Oil Pump Procedure, Install Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedure 007-031 (Lubricating Oil Pump) to to clarify the correct factory specification for measuring the oil pump gear backlash.</p>","tsb103917":"<h2>Engine Lifting Brackets Procedure, Multiple Section Revisions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedure 016-001 (Engine Lifting Brackets) in Section 16 of QSK45 and QSK60 Series Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>.</p><p>New capscrews are required after each removal of the engine lifting brackets.</p>","tsb103920":"<h2>Cylinder Head Procedure, Assemble Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the Assemble section of Procedure 002-004 (Cylinder Head). The valve guide installation service tool part numbers have been added.</p>"};
